        "offset": 0.3
      },
      "kind": "intro",
      "text": "Buck Ram, the Platters' manager, said he wrote The Great Pretender in about twenty minutes, in a Las Vegas hotel washroom.",
      "image": "artist-Q753905",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "The Great Pretender (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Great_Pretender"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "beatles-arrive",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 1,
        "offset": 2.1
      },
      "kind": "changeover",
      "text": "Please Please Me now sings over the Platters' band. John Lennon called it his attempt at a Roy Orbison song. George Martin sped it up.",
      "image": "artist-Q1299",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Please Please Me (song) (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Please_Please_Me_(song)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shania-arrives",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 3,
        "offset": 2.1
      },
      "kind": "changeover",
      "text": "Shania Twain now sings over the Beatles' band. She and Mutt Lange wrote You're Still the One to answer doubters of their marriage.",
      "image": "artist-Q131433",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "You're Still the One (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You%27re_Still_the_One"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "outro",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 4,
        "offset": 2.5
      },
      "kind": "outro",
      "text": "Lange added the counter-melody that became its hook. It cycles one, four, five, as this path does.",
      "image": "artist-Q131433",
      "sources": [
